                "ev-adcbc11ab31b-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Bergmann, the petitioner argues that reading paragraph\u202f6(3) in line with Congress\u2019s verb tense and the Court\u2019s decision in Tyler v. Cain shows the Government\u2019s interpretation is absurd and effectively nullifies the provision."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Bergmann",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "adcbc11ab31b85a21e0b66a7a9096f77c08166f55f00d90687393d44fe60d104",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-adcbc11ab31b-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 52,
                "start": 52
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Bergmann, the petitioner warns that the Government\u2019s proposal would rewrite the \u201cif\u201d clause by changing Congress\u2019s past\u2011tense verb to a future\u2011tense one."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Bergmann",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "adcbc11ab31b85a21e0b66a7a9096f77c08166f55f00d90687393d44fe60d104",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-adcbc11ab31b-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 56,
                "start": 56
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Bergmann, in closing, the petitioner argues that his interpretation best respects Congress\u2019s use of tense and aligns with the Court\u2019s reading in Tyler."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (Michael Donald Dodd)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
